{
  "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
  "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0000-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 2,
        "start": 2
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The above-entitled matter came on for oral argument before the Supreme Court of the United States at 10:06 a.m."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Franklin Taylor Rouse",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Congress created the Tennessee Valley Authority as a corporation that could sue and be sued. The TVA Act states: Except as otherwise specifically provided in this Act, the corporation may sue and be sued in its corporate name."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: I'm sorry. Are you denouncing the existence of a core government activity not being immunized?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0000-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 12,
        "start": 12
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: So how much does your argument rely on the sue-to-be-sued clause or -- or the exclusion of the TVA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kavanaugh",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0001-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 25,
        "start": 25
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KAVANAUGH: And are you -- just so I understand your argument here, are you asking us to simply hold that the right test is Burr, instead of discretionary function, and then to remand for application of Burr in the first instance by the court of appeals?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: I will go back for a second because I think that we have a statute, TVA exempt from the Federal Tort Claims Act. I thought the government is agreeing with you. Burr does apply. But Burr sometimes says that we have the equivalent of a Federal Tort Claims Act. Sometimes. Okay?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Sotomayor",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0001-0005",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 31,
        "start": 31
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SOTOMAYOR: Ms. O'Connell, is it, though? As Justice Alito pointed out, it is a hybrid entity. It does governmental functions and it does commercial functions. You'll have to explain to me why raising a power line is a government function."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Heritage Reporting Corporation",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0001-0006",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MS. O'CONNELL ADAMS: Well, people that -- that would like to sue the TVA back in 1942, the agency would have lost settlement authority at a thousand dollars. The -- the people would have to file a suit in federal district court and then negotiate with the Attorney General or the U.S. Attorney's Offices on terms set by Washington, D.C."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Ms. O'Connell Adams",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 46,
        "start": 46
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "Well, I think -- I guess the fact that Congress brought sue-and-be-sued agencies generally under the protection of the Federal Tort Claims Act shows that it didn't care what function the agency was performing, whether it was a commercial"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kagan",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 47,
        "start": 47
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "if -- if -- if I'm a Tennessee resident and I can't sue the TVA for this conduct, for raising a transmission line negligently, what kind of negligent suit can I bring against the TVA?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Alito",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0002-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 58,
        "start": 58
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And by \"this category of claim,\" what do you mean?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Breyer",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0003-0000",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 66,
        "start": 66
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE BREYER: What about the other\nsentence in Prosser: \"For example, activities\nof police or firefighters, though tortious, are\nusually considered governmental, in the sense\nthat they involve the kind of power expected of\ngovernment, even if its exercise in the\nspecific case is wrongful, the city is immune\nas to such activities for this reason.\""
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Chief Justice Roberts",
      "case_id": "2018-17-1201",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "c77e9dcc72d1063c1b7ac32f454d735de21ebcc13c66764b6cc5a2b4e050d249",
      "evidence_id": "ev-c77e9dcc72d1-0003-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 68,
        "start": 68
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "CHIEF JUSTICE ROBERTS: Thank you,\ncounsel. The case is submitted.\n(Whereupon, at 11:06 a.m., the case\nwas submitted.)"
    },
